            </profile>
            <profile id="bd2f-3918-cd8f-6cc7" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword and thrusting spear. May add javelins +2 pts. May have light armour at +3 pts, heavy armour at +4 pts. May have shield +3 pts. May ride a horse (free, increases Movement to 8, +1 save). Army General. Warband Psychology. Stealth. The Warlord is Stubborn and any unit (except Slave Warriors) attached to the General becomes Stubborn as well. The army must have a Warlord and he is the Army General. (Alexander the Great p.85)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="1532-122d-3f7b-9898" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
